# The self-hosted form's settings, read by docker-compose.yml (README, "Self-hosting"). Copy to
# `.env` beside it, then fill the three groups below. Everything here also reaches the graft
# container, so any server variable documented in packages/env/src/schema.ts may be added.

# 1. Secrets — Graft refuses to start without them. Mint all five at once with the image itself:
#      docker compose run --rm --no-deps graft node dist/keys.mjs >> .env
#    (or, from a checkout with pnpm: pnpm --filter @graft/server keys >> .env)
# GRAFT_AUTH_SECRET=
# GRAFT_KEYRING_SECRET=
# GRAFT_HANDOFF_SECRET=
# GRAFT_CAPABILITY_TOKEN_PRIVATE_KEY=
# GRAFT_CAPABILITY_TOKEN_PUBLIC_KEY=

# 2. The model that authors tools (ADR 0014: a self-host brings its own key). The provider group and
#    the rule that a production self-host refuses to start without it are GRA-31's. The provider is
#    `anthropic` or `openai`; the two model ids are optional and default per provider (for openai
#    the two shown; for anthropic claude-fable-5-1 and claude-haiku-4-5-20251001); the base URL
#    points the openai provider at an OpenAI-compatible gateway.
# GRAFT_MODEL_BACKEND=provider
# GRAFT_MODEL_PROVIDER=openai
# GRAFT_MODEL_API_KEY=
# GRAFT_MODEL_AUTHORING=gpt-5.6-sol
# GRAFT_MODEL_TRIAGE=gpt-5.4-mini
# GRAFT_MODEL_BASE_URL=

# Optional: Langfuse traces every model call acquire makes (GRA-31). The pair is all-or-nothing; the
# base URL names the region and defaults to the EU cloud.
# GRAFT_LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=
# GRAFT_LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=
# GRAFT_LANGFUSE_BASE_URL=

# 3. The admin opened on first start, into an empty database only. The compose file has development
#    defaults; set both before the console is reachable from anywhere but this machine.
GRAFT_ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com
GRAFT_ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me-before-exposing-this

# Where the console and the API answer, as the browser sees them. Behind a domain, the https origin.
GRAFT_PUBLIC_URL=http://localhost:3000
# Host ports. Postgres is published only for a server run from source on the host.
GRAFT_PORT=3000
GRAFT_POSTGRES_PORT=5432
# The Docker socket's group inside the graft container: 0 under Docker Desktop, on Linux the
# output of `stat -c %g /var/run/docker.sock`.
GRAFT_DOCKER_GID=0
# Which published images to run; a local build tags itself with the same name.
GRAFT_IMAGE_TAG=latest
